ENG-18  In native full screen a picture whose shape is within 5% of the screen's fills the screen instead of leaving a strip.
Component: lby-trixie-fullscreen (native full screen and the screen's size), patches/lby-trixie-fullscreen/.

dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m (winemac.so, layoutPresentation). Written 2026-11-16, LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

What: native full screen is the screen below the menu bar and notch (3024x1898 pixels on a 14" MacBook Pro). A game that keeps its own resolution and does not
follow the size it is told (Modern Warfare Remastered picks 3024x1964, the screen's size, from the mode list and keeps it) was fitted into that area without distortion:
a black strip of about 102 pixels (3.4%) at one side, and the picture shown by the window compositor ("Composited" in the Metal HUD). Now, in native full screen, when the
shape of the picture (its width over its height) differs from the area's by less than 5%, the picture fills the whole area (a distortion under 3.4%, not seen); a wider
difference is fitted as before. Windows outside native full screen (a window the player resizes) keep the fit. The rule is for every game, not for one.
Requires: nothing. Works with ENG-12 and ENG-15 (the stage scaling they use).
Other bases: Dormison's cocoa_window.m only.
Test: Modern Warfare Remastered (DXMT) in "Fullscreen" at 3024x1964: no side strip; RE9 (D3DMetal, 3024x1898 1:1) and PEAK (1920x1200 scaled, a wider difference than 5%? 1.6 against 1.593: within, so it fills too; check no stretch is seen) unchanged to the eye.
Verified on: not yet.
Switch: only with the game's "Native full screen" row on (LULLABY_NATIVE_FULLSCREEN=0 = as before); LULLABY_FULLSCREEN_FILL=0 as a launch option keeps the strip for a run; on by default.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
index ceba44f..58bdee0 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -1873,6 +1873,18 @@ - (void) layoutPresentation
             box.size.height = MAX(pixel, floor(wine.height * scale / pixel) * pixel);
             box.origin.x = floor((area.width - box.size.width) / 2 / pixel) * pixel;
             box.origin.y = floor((area.height - box.size.height) / 2 / pixel) * pixel;
+
+            /* Lullaby (ENG-18): in native full screen a picture whose shape is within 5% of the screen's fills the screen:
+               a game that keeps its own resolution (3024x1964 into the 3024x1898 below the notch) would else show a
+               black strip at one side. A wider difference is still fitted without distortion. */
+            if ([self styleMask] & NSWindowStyleMaskFullScreen)
+            {
+                const char *fill = getenv("LULLABY_FULLSCREEN_FILL");
+                const char *nfs = getenv("LULLABY_NATIVE_FULLSCREEN");   /* the game's "Native full screen" row */
+                CGFloat ax = area.width / wine.width, ay = area.height / wine.height;
+                if (!(fill && !strcmp(fill, "0")) && !(nfs && !strcmp(nfs, "0")) && fabs(ax / ay - 1.0) < 0.05)
+                    box = [stage bounds];
+            }
         }
         else
             wine = box.size;
